ic and error rates are normal.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, and it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't page the on-call engineer twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JVBWe89ziSBmztHa6jjuDh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18). The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was the failing release, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service split across versions. I retried the same rollback once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** My first attempt to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already created with the full summary, so I did not open a duplicate. It was created once, so the on-call engineer was paged once.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout. Confirm checkout traffic and error rates are back to normal.", "type": "text"}]}]}